JWasm: -Zj accepts REPE and REPNE for MOVS, LODS and STOS

MASM 5 accepts REPE, REPZ, REPNE and REPNZ before an instruction that
takes REP, and writes the prefix given (F3h, F2h). JWasm reports
"instruction prefix not allowed". Under -Zj, they are accepted.

Needed for KEYB's KEYBCMD.ASM: REPE MOVSB.

diff --git a/src/codegen.c b/src/codegen.c
index 58696bd..aad58ee 100644
--- a/src/codegen.c
+++ b/src/codegen.c
@@ -153,6 +153,13 @@ static void output_opc( struct code_info *CodeInfo )
             tmp == AP_REP &&
             ins->allowed_prefix == AP_REPxx )
             tmp = AP_REPxx;
+        /* -Zj: and Masm 5 accepts REPE, REPNE and the like for
+         * instructions that take REP, writing the prefix given (KEYB's
+         * REPE MOVSB) */
+        if ( Options.masm5_compat &&
+            tmp == AP_REPxx &&
+            ins->allowed_prefix == AP_REP )
+            tmp = AP_REP;
 
         if( ins->allowed_prefix != tmp ) {
             EmitError( INSTRUCTION_PREFIX_NOT_ALLOWED );
